  "world.gagan": { verdict: "corrected", on: "2026-10-07", rationale: "Re-checked on 7 October 2026 after the text changed. The ICAO APAC SBAS implementation guidance (Attachment A to the ITF/7 report, 2025) §2.4.1 gives APV-I availability of 99% 'over 76% of the Indian land mass excluding the period of solar storms on nominal days', and §2.5 quotes e-AIP India ENR 4.3: 'APV 1: 99% of time over 76% of Indian Landmass', 'RNP 0.1: 99% of time over 100% of Indian FIR'. The claim had said APV-I over the Indian landmass; corrected to 76% of it. §2.4 says INLUS uplinks the messages 'to three geostationary communication satellites GSAT-8, GSAT-10 and GSAT-15. The GEO satellites broadcast these correction messages', so the page now shows all three as operational; ENR 4.3 makes the service 'subject to availability of at least one GAGAN GEO Satellite' and no source read says whether one is a standby, as the note says. §2.4 also gives 15 reference stations and two master control centres. The years (2013, 2015), the three INLUS and the PRNs rest on the first pass (5 October 2026): ITF/7 IP/05b §1.1-1.2 and gps.gov PRN 127, 128, 132.", checked: [{"source": "ICAO APAC Guidance Document for Implementation of SBAS (ITF/7 report Attachment A, 2025)", "section": "§2.4, §2.4.1, §2.5 (e-AIP India ENR 4.3)", "read": true}, {"source": "ICAO APAC ITF/7 IP/05b (India, May 2025)", "section": "§1.1-1.2 (first pass)", "read": true}, {"source": "AAI GAGAN System presentation (Oct 2025)", "section": "DGCA actions, way forward (first pass)", "read": true}, {"source": "gps.gov L1 C/A PRN Code Assignments (Jan 2026)", "section": "PRN 127, 128, 132 (first pass)", "read": true}] },
